      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "This study examined the effect of administration with food on the ability of ranitidine bismuth citrate to suppress and eradicate Helicobacter pylori in 41 infected volunteers."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "After a 7-day course of treatment with ranitidine bismuth citrate (400 mg b.i.d.), 90% (18/20) of subjects who received the drug with food compared with 55% (11/20) of subjects who received the drug without food tested H. pylori-negative in a 13C-urea breath test (p = 0.031). Follow-up 13C-urea breath tests performed at least 3 months after therapy showed that H. pylori was eradicated in 14% (2/14) of subjects who received ranitidine bismuth citrate with food compared with 0% (0/18) of subjects who received ranitidine bismuth citrate without food (p = 0.183). The incidence of potentially drug-related adverse events was similar regardless of whether subjects received ranitidine bismuth citrate with or without food. Headache was the most common potentially drug-related adverse event."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "These data demonstrate that administration of ranitidine bismuth citrate with food compared with without food significantly improves the suppression of H. pylori in infected volunteers."
        }
      ]},
